# TwichUI: rules for every task

## Project
TwichUI is a World of Warcraft addon for WoW: Forever (Lua 5.1): a small, curated interface companion, not a UI replacement. Features are quiet and opt-in: no unasked-for chat, pop-ups or reminders, and never automated casting, item use, trading or selling. `CLAUDE.md` has the full rules; read only the section a task needs.

## Layout (verified; use it instead of searching)
Spelling: TwichUI (T-w-i-c-h, never "Twitch"). The core addon folder is `!!!TwichUI/` (three `!`).
- `!!!TwichUI/!!!TwichUI.toc`: load order. A core file not listed there never loads.
- `!!!TwichUI/Core.lua`: `R` (`local R = TwichUI`), events, `R.Print`, `DEFAULT_MODULES` (switch defaults), `COMMANDS` (`/tui`).
- `!!!TwichUI/Switches.lua`: what each switch does.
- Feature folders in `!!!TwichUI/`: `modules/`, `qol/`, `pins/`, `setup/`, `chronicle/`, `gear/`, `auction/`, `diag/`.
- `TwichUI_Settings/`: the settings window, a separate load-on-demand addon (`Kit.lua`, `pages/`, its own `.toc`).
- `tests/`: offline tests.
- Edit only files in `!!!TwichUI/`, `TwichUI_Settings/` and `tests/`, plus `TASK_NOTES.md`. Never edit `!!!TwichUI/libs/` or `!!!TwichUI/media/`.
- WoW API reference (read-only, outside the repo): `../wow-ui-source/`.

## Paths
- Copy every path exactly from this file, the user or tool output. Never retype or "fix" one. Use repo-relative paths.
- In terminal commands, single-quote paths with `!!!`: `'!!!TwichUI/Core.lua'`. Unquoted or in double quotes, the shell replaces `!!`.
- If a read or command fails, stop and show the exact error. Write code only for files you read in this task.
- Files over 300 lines: `grep -n 'name' '<file>'`, then read a range: `sed -n '120,180p' '<file>'`.
- `grep` exit code 1 means no match, not an error.

## Commands (from the repo root; verified)
- After every Lua edit: `luac5.1 -p '<file>'` (no output means OK). Never run plain `luac`.
- One test (any `tests/test_*.lua`): `(cd tests && lua5.1 -e 'require("bit"); ROOT="../!!!TwichUI/"; REPO="../"; TESTS="./"' test_qol.lua)`
- All tests (about 10 s): `./tests/run.sh`
- No lint exists. Unless the user asks, never run `tools/` scripts, deploys, `git commit` or `git push`.

## Hard rules
1. Use a WoW API or event only after finding it in this repo or `../wow-ui-source/`. Not found: say so and stop.
2. Lua 5.1: `local` for everything, no new globals, no `goto`, `//` or bitwise operators.
3. `R:On("EVENT", fn)`: `fn` gets only the event's payload, never `self, event`. Undo with `R:Off("EVENT", fn)`.
4. Secure frames and protected actions can't change in combat: check `InCombatLockdown()`, redo the work on `PLAYER_REGEN_ENABLED`.
5. Saved values go only through the feature's `Get`/`Set` (switches: `R:Enabled`, `R:SetEnabled`). Never rename a saved key.
6. Settings rows go in `TwichUI_Settings/pages/`, never Blizzard's options. Open the window with `R:OpenSettings(page)`.
7. Chat: `R.Print("text %s", value)`, only in answer to the player's own command or click.
8. Write complete code: no stubs or placeholder comments. If you can't finish, stop and say what is missing.
9. Make the smallest change that works: no renaming, reformatting or cleanup. Never change `## Interface` or `## Version` in a `.toc`.
10. Ask before adding a library or copied code. Never use `loadstring` or `load`.

## How to work
1. Read `TASK_NOTES.md`, then the matching recipe, then only the files it names.
2. Before editing, state in 2 or 3 lines which files and functions you will change, and why. Research or planning request: change no file except `TASK_NOTES.md`.
3. Edit one file at a time, run `luac5.1 -p` on it, then update `TASK_NOTES.md`. More than 3 files: list the steps under `Next` first.
4. Finish with the recipe's tests, then `./tests/run.sh`.
5. Unsure, stuck, or about to repeat a search or an edit: stop and ask one specific question.

## TASK_NOTES.md (survives context compaction)
Repo root, gitignored; create it if missing. Read it at the start of every task and right after any context compaction. Update it after every edit and every verified fact. Rewrite, don't append; under 40 lines; exactly these sections: `## Goal`, `## Done` (path, function), `## Facts` (verified paths, APIs, line ranges), `## Next` (1 to 3 steps), `## Open questions`. Record only what a file or tool output showed; mark the rest `UNVERIFIED`. If notes and code disagree, trust the code. When the task is finished, replace everything with `No active task.`

## Final report
Files changed (path, function); what changed and why; commands run and their results; what to test in game after `/reload`; risks and open questions. Never claim a check you did not run.

## Recipes (read the matching one before you start)
- `docs/recipes/add-switch.md`: on/off checkbox
- `docs/recipes/add-feature-setting.md`: slider, dropdown, color, feature option
- `docs/recipes/add-settings-page.md`: new page, page keys
- `docs/recipes/add-module.md`: new feature file, events, combat
- `docs/recipes/add-slash-command.md`: `/tui` command
- `docs/recipes/wow-api-lookup.md`: any WoW API or event
- `docs/recipes/food-drink-module.md`: before editing `!!!TwichUI/modules/FoodDrink.lua`
